149:The Lost Treasure
150:Even after securing the giant tile dubbed the Sacred Tile by that mysterious voice, the situation remains perilous.
151:Frieren
152:Fern, watch our heads.
153:Fern
154:Leave it to me, Ms. Frieren.
155:Ichihime
156:Whoa, that defensive magic came out so fast, nyaa! Just as snappy as my All Simples, nyaa!
157:Fern casts defensive spells in rapid succession to intercept the falling debris, her aim never wavering even as she sprints.
158:Stark carves a path through the front with his axe, while Übel effortlessly cuts whatever obstacles remain.
159:Working together, we finally reach the exit.
161:Yuzu
162:Argh?! What happened to you guys? Look at this mess!
163:I have no idea, nyaa! The ruins just started collapsing out of nowhere, nyaa!
164:Maybe this is the Sacred Tile's doing again, nyaa...
165:Leia
166:At least everyone made it out unscathed.
167:I bet this tile holds the key to fixing everything, nyaa! Even if I don't quite know how it works yet...
168:Bringing it back with us is definitely the right play, nyaa!
169:???
170:N-no, you can't...
171:Hand it back... the Sacred Tile! You can't take it!
172:If you give it back, I'll trade you anything else you want...
173:Pearls, coral, tasty treats – anything!
175:Who are...
177:Lin Lang?
178:Is she someone you know?
179:Well, nyaa... She definitely sounds like Lin Lang, a close friend of ours who happens to be a dragon.
180:But something feels totally off about her, nyaa...
181:player
182:Wait, no! She's an imposter!
183:After all, Lin Lang would never willingly part with tasty treats.
184:Indeed, nyaa! The real Lin Lang would never do something like this in the first place, nyaa!
185:I see... An imposter, then.
186:On closer inspection, the figure resembling Lin Lang is shrouded in fog and doesn't seem to have a solid form.
187:Could she be... a mirage?
188:How sneaky, disguising as a little girl so we'd let our guard down, nyaa!
189:I didn't... I just...
190:So you're the big bad demon king pulling strings behind this fog, nyaa?
191:You better not try anything funny, nyaa! Just give yourself up, nyaa!
192:Demon king...? I don't know anything like that! I'm not a demon king!
193:But... if you don't return the Sacred Tile, I'll... I'll...
194:I'll trap you all in the fog forever!
195:Übel
197:By the way, you have such lovely hair... I bet it'll make a delightful sound when I snip through it.
198:Eek...!
199:Übel's "tender loving care" leaves the girl on the verge of tears.
200:If you're not the Demon King, why not step aside?
201:We're not bad guys, but this Sacred Tile is crucial.
202:You... really don't seem like one... Wait, no...
203:Even so, she stands her ground before us, trembling all over.
204:No, no! I... I can't let fear take over now!
205:That person taught me...!
206:Help me, Guardians of the Sacred Tile!
207:Guardian
208:!!!
209:Ichihime & Stark
210:A giant golem just showed up (nyaa)!!!
212:Looks like this won't be an easy fight.
213:Let's follow Master {var:player_nickname}'s advice and build a winning hand through our attacks.
214:A mahjong tile is knocked flying.
215:Yet the surrounding fog immediately coalesces to fill the gap, forming a block with a different tile pattern. The hand is still nowhere near complete.
216:The tile changed. A continuous assault might work better.
217:Ugh... You already figured out how the Guardians work?
218:But I can't give up...
219:Double Riichi!
220:Ngh?!
221:Unexpectedly, the monster splits in two, lunging from both sides at once.
222:Stark
223:Hey! Not only is this thing not going down, but it's multiplying?!
224:Does that hand even have yaku, nyaa?! Stop cheating, nyaa!
225:Damn it, so it's forcefully blocking us from declaring a win?!
226:Then, to completely shatter these monsters...
227:Th-there has to be a way, nyaa!
228:No matter how terrible the hand, victory is always possible... Mahjong is a realm of imagination, nyaa!
229:Imagination...
230:Indeed. Rather than assuming the enemy set an airtight board or played dirty...
231:The more likely truth is –
233:There actually is a yaku!
235:It's a special winning condition!
236:What did you figure out, Master?
237:A hand that seems yakuless yet ties into Double Riichi...
238:It's the local yaku Ishinouenimosannen (Three Years on a Stone), isn't it?
239:H-how did you... Eek!
240:Even so, realizing this does nothing to tip the scales in our current fight.
241:The other condition for this local yaku is pulling off Under the Sea.
242:Exactly... If we stall all the way to the final draw, you'll never hold out!
243:So just surrender...
244:Oh? Is that so? But I don't think staying like this is all that bad.
245:I can still fight.
246:Stark, keep holding them off. Can you do that?
247:...You just love bossing me around, huh?
248:Still, the odds are hardly in our favor.
249:Damn it, how are we even supposed to defeat...
250:Wait. Defeat?
252:Why do we have to win the hand?
254:Why can't we fold?
255:Declaring a win is just one way to knock the tiles over – it was never our real objective here.
256:All that matters is making the tiles fall.
257:I've got it!
258:Frieren, Fern, Übel... and Yuzu.
259:I'm counting on you!
260:You've come up with a plan, haven't you?
261:Tell us what to do, Master {var:player_nickname}.
262:What's the plan? Are we taking them down?
264:We don't need to defeat them.
266:Mahjong is a realm of imagination.
267:Everyone, strike the monsters on my mark – all at once!
268:Three!
269:Argh... I don't quite get how this works, but as the Witch of Justice, I'm ready to give it my all!
270:Two!
271:This trick of yours sounds pretty fun, {var:player_nickname}.
272:One!
273:I will give it everything I have!
274:Now!
275:<color=#6CC2B6>Zoltraak!</color>
276:Blasts from all four staffs strike the monsters' defenses at the exact same moment.
277:I-it's useless!
278:Brute force won't beat me...!
279:You're wrong.
280:This isn't brute force, and we're not trying to beat you...
281:Draw!
282:The moment the call rings out, the monsters freeze as if bound by magic.
284:If two golems count as Double Riichi, it's only logical that four spell strikes from the same direction would trigger a Four-Wind Discarded.
285:Sunlight finally bathes the island, dispelling the shroud of fog that once entombed it.
286:Th-that's impossible! Ugh...
287:Though she grits her teeth in frustration, without her Guardians, she's completely out of moves.
288:Can we calm down and talk this over now?
289:Exactly, nyaa! Why interfere with my heroic quest to save the world, nyaa?!
290:Even if this Sacred Tile belongs to you, you shouldn't use its power to stir up trouble.
291:S-stir up trouble...?
292:A look of innocent confusion crosses her face – she doesn't seem to be pretending.
293:We briefly fill her in on what has transpired.
295:Regardless, the spreading fog is no small matter.
297:Why did you do this?
298:B-because...
299:Her voice trails off, at a loss for words.
300:It's okay. Tell us what's on your mind.
301:Sensing she isn't inherently evil, I think there might be a genuine reason behind her actions.
302:After wrestling with her thoughts, she finally opens her mouth.
303:Truth is... I –

308:Then, their forms fade away completely.
309:Whew, nyaa... My heart is practically leaping out of my chest, nyaa...
312:Things are getting interesting... Though I'd rather not be trapped here.
